    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), who represents our most potent play. Facing Rea, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 33% combined boost from favorable park factors and pitching quality, making him an automatic anchor despite the minor penalty for the pitcher\u2019s ability to control the running game. **Kyle Tucker** (77.36) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) also rate as top-tier starts against Gabriel Hughes and Cabrera respectively; both benefit from an excellent matchup against a pitcher with an xERA over 5.00, providing an elite floor for the outfield corps. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) rounds out our primary tier, as he capitalizes on a strong platoon advantage against Arrighetti that elevates his production profile significantly.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Brayan Rocchio** (51.40). He was the clear lead candidate to displace **Sam Antonacci** (43.42) or **Liam Hicks** (48.77), but the optimizer favored the plate appearance volume of the starting lineup, particularly given the favorable lineup slots for our core infielders. Risk remains elevated for players like **Heliot Ramos** (45.17), who faces the elite arm of Cease; while wind conditions offer a slight reprieve, the raw SP skill gap makes him a marginal play. We are also monitoring \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**; if any of these stars drop significantly in the batting order once official lineups are posted, their projected efficiency scores will be subject to immediate downward revision, potentially triggering a shuffle with the remaining bench options like **Jorge Polanco** or **Josh Lowe**.",
